Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Review lows: the crossing leads its message; the
 parallel test checks the tips and says what the distributed layout checks

- The refusal for a chain that crosses or touches an unrecorded fault's
  sides now names the crossing first and the piece count as its
  consequence; test_0897 matches the whole leading clause.
- The comment and add_fault's Raises say that any pair of labels <n>Plus
  and <n>Minus is taken as a fault's sides, by name alone.
- The parallel test asserts, for every trace it adds, that both tips are
  vertices of the fault (reduced over the ranks), and its docstring says
  that distributed, most traces meet the seam refusal first, so for those
  the layout checks only that the ranks agree.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
